~ Lava slice 10 — bounds: refinements declared on a container.
~ A bound is part of the container's identity, so the bad state cannot exist.

~ literal bound: balance can never go negative
create container "Credit" of type int at least 0 with value 100

~ relational bound: a hold can never exceed the credit backing it
create container "Hold" of type int never above Credit with value 0

~ legal moves
update Credit to [Credit - 40]      ~ 60, still >= 0
update Hold to 60                    ~ 60, not above Credit (60)
print(Credit)
print(Hold)

~ a guarded effect that respects the bound
if (Credit is 60) then update Hold to [Hold - 10]
print(Hold)

~ the bad state is structurally impossible. The next line, if run, fails:
~   update Credit to -5            ~ would violate `at least 0`
~   update Hold to 999             ~ would violate `never above Credit`
~ See bounds-violation.lava for the rejection, and bounds-atomic.lava for how
~ a synchronous block may pass through an intermediate dip and still commit.
